\[ 12 \times 62 = 12 \times (60 + 2) \]

Now, distribute the 12:

\[ 12 \times (60 + 2) = (12 \times 60) + (12 \times 2) \]

Next, we calculate each term separately.

\[ 12 \times 60 = 720 \]
